ally happens  and it's a matter for the chief whip uh  not for me but what usually happens is  an investigation will follow there will  be be inquiry she will be spoken to I  don't know how long all of those things  will take and what that will mean for  her her future but but losing the whip  so therefore no longer being recognized  as a labor MP is an incredibly serious  sanction and one which uh the chief Whip  and kissed armor as as leader are  unafraid to take when someone does  something as wrong as this no I  understand but I just wondered what what  your view was you say that it was a  racist comment I mean should a racist be  allowed back into the party  well it was a as I say it was a wrong  and racist and and you know entirely  misjudged uh comment and she's already  paying a a heavy price for that and what  happens to her in the future is not my  decision it's one that will get looked  at uh properly by by the chief whip in  consultation with other people and that  is something that that they should deal  with I don't think it probably helps for  me to comment on that further I don't  know I mean you are representing the  labor party here this morning Ms Paul  and you know by all accounts um people  suggesting that you will be in power  before too long it's a reasonable  question should somebody who makes  racist comments be welcome by the labor  party  I think someone who makes comments like  these should face very serious sanction  rupa's already faced uh serious sanction  that will continue  um I don't know how that will be  resolved if it would be resolved or  whether she would be allowed back in the  party but I think what your viewers  should know is that we take these  matters incredibly seriously we act  swiftly uh you know without making this  a sort of you know party political point  I think that does stand in stark  contrast to what we've seen with Boris  Johnson and the conservatives recently  where they don't stand up and take  action agains